<title>USA: U.S. propane stocks post gains for second week.</title>
<headline>U.S. propane stocks post gains for second week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. inventories of propane continued to post gains for the second consecutive week, up 1.1 million barrels to 25.2 million, the weekly EIA report showed Wednesday.</p>
<p>The gain for the week ended March 28, 1997 maintained U.S. inventories within the lower limit of normal range for this time of year, the Energy Information Administration report said.</p>
<p>Regionally, the major producing hub of the U.S. Gulf Coast rose 500,000 barrels to 11.35 million and the Midwest gained 800,000 barrels to 9.8 million.</p>
<p>The East Coast dipped 200,000 to 3.2 million, the EIA report said.</p>
<p>--Laney Salisbury, New York Energy Desk 1212 859-1631</p>
